Adds docs/investigations/stance_2026_10/critic_blind_results/ with
run_log.txt, lines 760 to 801 of the session's run log (the entries
timed 23:47 UTC on 2026-10-29 to 16:32 UTC on 2026-10-30), the
overnight report the maintainer read before choosing the second screen
(MORNING_REPORT.md, a byte copy), and a README naming the decision
entries. The run log holds #653's opening, CI and merge; the
maintainer's answers of 00:24 and 00:45 UTC (the early-bias probe, then
the overnight authorisation); the early-bias probe, run and verified
with corrections; the early-warning curve and its two follow-ups (the
r9 held-out test and the margin-to-rail test), verified, with an
incident at about 01:05 UTC (an agent replaced the system's /dev/null
with a regular file for about 1 to 2 minutes, restored at 01:06 UTC;
the probe's logs show no error in that window); the intervention chosen
at 04:22 UTC; the first critic-blind screen's scaffold, pin, launch,
check-ins, reading (line 1, not informative), independent check,
APPROVED's full text and durable copy; #654's opening and CI; the
maintainer's answer of 10:23 UTC (option A); the second screen's build
and criteria, its pin at the answer of 12:53 UTC, launch, check-ins,
reading (line 2, reduced), independent check, report and durable copy;
#654's merge; and the maintainer's answers of 16:23 UTC, with the long
study's build launched at 16:32 UTC. It was copied at about 16:36 UTC,
when the source had 802 lines; line 802 (16:33 UTC) starts this
records change, and it and every later line go to a later records
change.

It continues ecs_results/run_log.txt (lines 721 to 759) with no line
in both. As the earlier copies were made: lines (the sha256 given is
that of the source's first 801 lines, 35b00201...; its first 759 lines
are unchanged, f2a95d7b..., the value the ecs_results copy's row gives)
and redact (16 workflow run ids, 9 distinct, a bare one becoming
'workflow [id removed]'; 3 scheduled-task ids, 2 distinct; and the
assistant's name in a GitHub check's name, as the stance4 and stance5
run-log copies did); these lines hold no checkout path, Drive id or
task-list id. The overnight report is byte-identical; its copy on the
first screen's durable branch (claude/handoff-bias-screen at cfed2c70,
FOR_THE_MAINTAINER.md) lacks §4's last bullet, added after that push.
No new kind of change. SOURCES.txt gains the note and two rows;
SHA256SUMS now pins 1366 files (sha256sum -c: all OK); the folder's
README gains the entry, the folder's note under "What changed in the
copies", its README among the files SHA256SUMS does not pin, and four
re-check rows, and this change's status row names the folder.

Records only: no library code, configuration, test, notebook, digest or
generated file changes.

